SARAH 128 - KEY HELP
===================

CS = CAPS SHIFT, SS = SYMBOL SHIFT

DIRECTORY
---------
Up / Down   Move the cursor
Left/Right  Change directory page
ENTER       Open directory or supported file
BREAK       Go to parent directory
I           Find an item
X           Scroll a long item name
SPACE       Mark or unmark the item
CS+M        Mark all items
SS+M        Unmark all items
R           Read the directory again
6           Rename the item
7           Create a directory
DELETE      Delete the item
N           Switch LIST / NLST
SS+N        Switch abbreviated / full listing
Z           View any file as text

TEXT VIEWER
-----------
Left        Previous screen
Right       Next screen
BREAK       Return to Sarah

ENTER opens TXT and POK files in the same viewer.
For CFG or other files, use Z.
Viewing downloads into memory; it does not save a file.
Non-printable bytes appear as dots. TAB is one space.
Files over 65535 bytes are shown only up to that limit.
A warning is displayed before downloading a large file.

FTP AND SETTINGS
----------------
L           Log in
SS+L        Automatic login sequence
O           Log off
H           Set FTP host
E           Set user name
P           Set password
SS+P        Toggle password visibility
A           Toggle automatic login
F           Set default file name
T           Set file start address
S           Show file size
U           Upload
D           Download selected / marked files to disk
CS+D        Download a file by entering its name
SS+D        Download the default file
B           Abort a running download
C           Send an FTP command
G           Choose a CFG profile; ENTER logs in (BS-DOS)
K           Open local sara.hlp (BS-DOS, no FTP needed)
W           Toggle Wi-Fi state on exit
V           Save the application
Q           Quit Sarah

OPENING FILES (BS-DOS)
---------------------
ENTER on TAP downloads, extracts and starts the program.
The original TAP is currently kept after extraction.
ENTER on SNA / Z80 downloads and hands it to the NMI menu.
An unsupported NMI menu shows a message and returns.

Keep sara.hlp next to sara.cfg on the current BS-DOS disk.
Press K to open it, Left/Right to browse and BREAK to return.
